2. Numerically compatible re-implementations.
   The preprocessing engine contains independent C++ re-implementations written to reproduce, bit for bit,
   the numerical behaviour of these libraries' routines, for parity with the Python reference pipeline:
   - OpenCV 4.13: cv::resize, cv::cvtColor RGB2GRAY and CascadeClassifier. OpenCV is licensed under Apache-2.0.
   - Pillow 11.3: Image.resize BILINEAR. Pillow is licensed under MIT-CMU (HPND).
   - FFmpeg 6.1 swscale: unscaled yuv420p -> rgb24 arithmetic. FFmpeg is licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later.
   No source files of these projects are included. The source comments name the routines each
   implementation matches. Their trademarks belong to their respective owners.

3. Model architectures.
   SHIELD-V (MobileNetV3-Large frame encoder + GDN/SISA sequence stages) and SHIELD-A were designed and trained
   by the SHIELD team. oracle/shieldv_ref.py is an independent PyTorch re-implementation used as a numerical
   reference. MobileNetV3 is described in Howard et al., "Searching for MobileNetV3" (ICCV 2019).
